<title>USA: IBM eyes job buyouts for up to 5,000 - NYT.</title>
<headline>IBM eyes job buyouts for up to 5,000 - NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Business Machines Corp is planning to offer job buyouts, or inducements to shift jobs, to between 3,000 and 5,000 employees, the New York Times reported Tuesday.</p>
<p>The voluntary plan could be presented this week, the article said, quoting unnamed sources.</p>
<p>The employees would be offered cash to leave the company or incentives to transfer to other jobs at the company's fastest-growing divisions.</p>
<p>IBM is not expected to take a charge against earnings to implement the plans, the article said.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk  (212) 859-1610</p>
</text>
